## Experiment 9 — Stored Procedures

1. Write a MySQL program to create a Book table with the attributes id, title, price, and ISBN. Insert sample records.
2. Create a stored procedure to display all the records from the table.
3. Write a MySQL stored procedure using IN parameters to update the price of a book based on its ISBN number. Display the updated records.
4. Write a MySQL stored procedure using an OUT parameter to find the maximum price of books stored in the Book table. Display the highest price using a user-defined session variable.
5. Write a MySQL stored procedure using an INOUT parameter to retrieve the current price of a book, increase it by ₹500, update the table, and display the new price.

